TARGA RESOURCES CORP. STATEMENT OF POSITION IN LIEU OF TESTIMONY

       Pursuant to the Hearings Examiners’ Order Revising Procedural Deadlines issued June 18,

2026, Targa Resources Corp. (“Targa”) respectfully submits this Statement of Position in Lieu of

Testimony regarding the Comprehensive Stipulation of parties filed on June 22, 2026

(“Stipulation”) in this case. In support thereof, Targa respectfully asserts the following:

       1.     Customer growth in service area of Southwestern Public Service Company (“SPS”)

has dramatically increased and will continue to grow driven primarily by rapid economic

development in the region. Yet several of SPS’s thermal units are at or near retirement. In addition,

planning-reserve margin requirements within the Southwest Power Pool have dramatically

increased. SPS and its customers have an urgent need for new generation to ensure SPS is able to

serve new load, fulfill its duty to customers, and meet its obligations.


                                                  1
        2.     Targa participated in settlement negotiations among the parties in this case. Targa

found the negotiations to be conducted in good faith and were very productive, leading to a fair

resolution among joining parties and a sound recommendation for the Commission.

       3.     The Stipulation provides a just and reasonable resolution of contested issues among

the parties. The agreed revenue requirement and related capital structure and rate of return on

investment will enable SPS to address the provide safe and reliable service to customers, while

also providing reasonable and meaningful customer protections and other benefits.

       Wherefore, Targa prays for Commission to adopt orders necessary to enact the terms of the

Stipulation to support SPS’s efforts to construct and operate new generation resources and related

measures, along with the agreed reasonable customer protections, and to grant all other further

relief as this Commission deems just and proper.



                                              Respectfully submitted,

